<title>POLAND: ESPEBEPE ENJOYS 9.7 PCT SPECULATIVE SURGE.</title>
<headline>ESPEBEPE ENJOYS 9.7 PCT SPECULATIVE SURGE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Espebepe SA surged 9.7 percent to 7.35 zlotys in speculative trade as the stock had no fundamental reason to jump with the company facing a bankruptcy threat, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's clearly speculation,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Some traders linked the speculation with the company's March 14 creditors meeting, where a possible debt write-off deal will be discussed. Espebepe owes 80 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Buying after price-fixing on Monday was strong enough for investors to have their bids reduced.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
